inked ?origin_availability ?payload_unit)). No effect on origin_node_ready. So origin_node_ready unchanged. So if origin_node_ready was true before loading, it stays true after loading. Similarly unload_origin_payload sets origin_node_ready and clears occupied. So we can have origin_node_ready true before loading, then load payload making occupied true while ready stays true. Then we have both occupied and ready true. Good. So we need origin_node_ready true before loading.

