Dispatch_ready actions: mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready (requires origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready). Similarly for destination. For schedule candidate: there is execute_schedule_dispatch? No, that's for dispatch after allocation. There's also mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready. For schedule candidate, there is no explicit mark_dispatch_ready action; but we can get dispatch_ready via finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation or finalize_candidate_direct or finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation, which set dispatch_ready as effect. Indeed finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation effect includes dispatch_ready ?candidate. Also finalize_candidate_direct effect includes dispatch_ready. Also finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation effect includes dispatch_ready. So we can make shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_ready via finalizing it. Similarly shift_candidate_beta? Goal does not require dispatch_ready for shift_candidate_beta. So we don't need.

